    "q-80767": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80767",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xy-yz-xz$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y-z)\\text{ }i+(x-z)\\text{ }j+(-y-x)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,4) & =(3-4)\\text{ }i+(2-4)\\text{ }j+(-3-2)k \\\\  & =-1\\text{ }i-2\\text{ }j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)-2(y-3)-5(z-4) & =0 \\\\ -x-2y-5z+28 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+5z-28 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
