    "q-102708": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102708",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-1,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{3}z-xy+x{z}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =({z}^{3}-y)\\text{ }i+(3z{y}^{2}-x)\\text{ }j+(3x{z}^{2}+{y}^{3})k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-1,1) & =({1}^{3}-(-1))\\text{ }i+(3(1)(-1)^{2}-2)\\text{ }j+(3(2)(1)^{2}+(-1)^{3})k \\\\  & =2\\,i+\\,j+5k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,1,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-102708-a",
