    "q-80769": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80769",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,1,1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+8y\\text{ }j+4z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+8(1)j+4(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+8\\,j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,8,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,8,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)+8(y-1)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x+8y+4z-20 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
