    "q-102707": {
      "dom_id": "step-q102707",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,-1).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z+{z}^{2}y+{y}^{2}x)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xz+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+({z}^{2}+2yx)\\text{ }j+({x}^{2}+2zy)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,-1) & =(2(1)(-1)+{1}^{2})\\text{ }i+((-1)^{2}+2(1)(1))\\text{ }j+({1}^{2}+2(-1)(1))k \\\\  & =-\\,i+3\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)+3(y-1)-(z+1) & =0 \\\\ -x+3y-z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-102707-a",
